# Ship = commit + push + deploy

When Jon asks to **commit and push** (or "sube", "ship", "manda"), do **all three** in order:

1. Commit (never `.env`; HEREDOC message; no amend/force unless explicitly asked)
2. `git push` to `origin`
3. `fly deploy` (app `kore`) — do **not** stop after push and ask whether to deploy

**No esperes a que Fly termine.** El deploy tarda y atasca el chat. Lánzalo en background (`block_until_ms: 0`) y **sigue** con lo siguiente. No hagas poll / AwaitShell del deploy.

Reporta: commit hash, push OK, deploy lanzado → https://kore.fly.dev/

Exception: only skip deploy if Jon says explicitly "solo commit/push, sin deploy".
